/-!
# Actual restriction of a holomorphic period family

For every original holomorphic period map and every open subset of its base,
the restricted original period functions define a genuine quotient family.
On an analytic complex base, this family is biholomorphic to the full
preimage of that open set in the original total space. The source quotient
atlas and target inherited open atlas are retained without alteration.

The equivalence is literal pair regrouping and preserves the actual covering
maps, projections, zero sections and original complex period-torus inclusions.
It is natural under nested base-open inclusions, which are holomorphic maps
of the actual restricted families and obey the identity and composition laws.

No higher-cohomology or derived base-change assertion is made here.
-/
